{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TowerSpanReduction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TowerSpanReduction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.DisjointBlockTraceLaw"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TowerSpanReduction.disjointBlock_of_sandwichReduces","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TowerSpanReduction.disjointBlock_of_sandwichReduces","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TowerSpanReduction.lean#L202-L213","doc":"**The end-to-end statement.** The disjoint-block law follows from the local\nrewriting rule alone (plus the quadratic relation), by composing this file's\nreduction with `DisjointBlockTraceLaw.disjointBlock_of_towerSpan`.\n\n🛑 Still conditional: `SandwichReduces` is not proved for any tower with a\ngrowing filtration. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TowerSpanReduction.towerSpan_of_sandwichReduces","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TowerSpanReduction.towerSpan_of_sandwichReduces","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TowerSpanReduction.lean#L194-L200","doc":"**`TowerSpan` follows from the single local rewriting rule**, at every level\nat once. Pure repackaging of `step_of_sandwichReduces`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TowerSpanReduction.step_of_sandwichReduces","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TowerSpanReduction.step_of_sandwichReduces","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TowerSpanReduction.lean#L160-L192","doc":"**One filtration step decomposes, from the single local rewriting rule.**\n\nThe global decomposition at level `M` is implied by the local fact that\n`g (M+1) * c * g (M+1)` reduces, for `c` in the previous stage. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TowerSpanReduction.P_mul_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TowerSpanReduction.P_mul_mem","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TowerSpanReduction.lean#L144-L158","doc":"`P` is closed under multiplication once sandwiches reduce. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TowerSpanReduction.span_mul_span","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TowerSpanReduction.span_mul_span","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TowerSpanReduction.lean#L133-L142","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TowerSpanReduction.gen_mul_span","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TowerSpanReduction.gen_mul_span","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TowerSpanReduction.lean#L117-L131","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TowerSpanReduction.SandwichReduces","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TowerSpanReduction.SandwichReduces","kind":"def","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TowerSpanReduction.lean#L110-L115","doc":"**The reduction hypothesis.** A doubled generator with base material between\nit collapses back into `P`. This is the one blocking shape identified in\n`DisjointBlockTraceLaw`, and in the Hecke case it is where the braid relation\ndoes its work. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TowerSpanReduction.mul_base_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TowerSpanReduction.mul_base_right","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TowerSpanReduction.lean#L95-L108","doc":"Right multiplication by a base element preserves `P`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TowerSpanReduction.mul_base_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TowerSpanReduction.mul_base_left","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TowerSpanReduction.lean#L80-L93","doc":"Left multiplication by a base element preserves `P`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TowerSpanReduction.gen_mem_P","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TowerSpanReduction.gen_mem_P","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TowerSpanReduction.lean#L76-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TowerSpanReduction.base_le_P","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TowerSpanReduction.base_le_P","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TowerSpanReduction.lean#L73-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TowerSpanReduction.P","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TowerSpanReduction.P","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TowerSpanReduction.lean#L69-L71","doc":"The base together with single sandwiches, as a 